# Container image CVE exceptions — v8.13.33
# Reviewed: 2026-07-21  |  Re-review: each release cycle
# All entries are base-image (bitnami/minideb:bookworm) CVEs with no
# upstream fix available in Debian bookworm. Trivy status column is
# "affected" or "will_not_fix" for each.
# See docs/security-review.md#container-image-scanning for full rationale.

# zlib1g CVE-2023-45853 — CRITICAL, Debian will_not_fix
# Integer overflow in inflate(). Only exploitable when processing
# attacker-controlled deflate streams with a specific window size.
# curl and git in this image decompress only trusted responses from
# operator-configured remotes. Not network-exposed via datawatch APIs.
CVE-2023-45853

# libsqlite3-0 — no fix in bookworm (3 CVEs, 1 CRITICAL + 2 HIGH)
# SQLite is used internally by the gh CLI binary; not exposed via
# datawatch REST/MCP APIs. Processes only trusted local state.
#   CVE-2025-7458 (CRITICAL): Integer overflow in SQLite. No fix in bookworm.
#   CVE-2026-11822 (HIGH): Memory corruption in FTS5 full-text search extension
#     via crafted FTS5 page data (out-of-bounds read). Exploitable only against
#     attacker-controlled SQLite databases; gh CLI processes only trusted local
#     state (cached GitHub data), not attacker-supplied databases.
#   CVE-2026-11824 (HIGH): Heap buffer overflow in FTS5 via crafted continuation
#     page causing integer underflow. Same surface as CVE-2026-11822.
CVE-2025-7458
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824

# curl / libcurl4 — no fix in bookworm (2 HIGH)
#   CVE-2026-5773: Wrong file transfer via SMB protocol. SMB is not
#     used by curl in this image (no SMB server configured).
#   CVE-2026-6276: Cookie leak on cross-origin redirect. curl is used
#     by agent tooling for REST API calls; operator-configured endpoints.
CVE-2026-6276

# libldap-2.5-0 CVE-2023-2953 — HIGH, no fix in bookworm
# Null pointer dereference in ber_memalloc_x via malformed LDAP response.
# OpenLDAP not directly used; pulled transitively by OpenSSH. No LDAP
# connections made from within the container.
CVE-2023-2953

# ncurses CVE-2025-69720 — HIGH, no fix in bookworm
# (affects libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base)
# Buffer overflow in terminal escape sequence parsing. Triggerable only
# by attacker-controlled terminal output inside a tmux session. Requires
# prior container shell access.
CVE-2025-69720

# perl / perl-base / perl-modules-5.36 / libperl5.36 — no fix in bookworm (6 CVEs)
# Perl is installed as a transitive dependency (git and gnupg pull it in).
# The datawatch service does not execute Perl scripts or call Archive::Tar.
#   CVE-2026-42496 (CRITICAL): Archive::Tar symlink traversal during extraction.
#     Only exploitable if Archive::Tar is called to extract a malicious tar.
#     datawatch does not extract tar archives at runtime.
#   CVE-2026-42497 (HIGH): Archive::Tar hardlink traversal. Same surface.
#   CVE-2026-48962 (HIGH): perl-IO-Compress arbitrary code execution via
#     crafted compressed input. datawatch does not decompress via IO::Compress.
#   CVE-2026-8376 (HIGH): heap buffer overflow in Perl interpreter. Requires
#     running attacker-supplied Perl code; no Perl execution in container.
#   CVE-2026-9538 (HIGH): Archive::Tar memory corruption. Same as CVE-2026-42496.
#   CVE-2026-48959 (HIGH): IO::Uncompress::Unzip CPU exhaustion via malformed
#     zip file. datawatch does not decompress zip files via Perl at runtime;
#     Perl is only present as a transitive dependency of git.
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-9538

# git-lfs CVE-2025-26625 — HIGH, no fix available
# git-lfs may write to arbitrary files via crafted LFS pointer refs returned
# by a malicious LFS server. Only exploitable when cloning/pulling from an
# attacker-controlled git remote. All git remotes in this image are
# operator-configured; no untrusted LFS servers are contacted.
CVE-2025-26625

# python3.11 / libpython3.11-* — no fix in bookworm (3 CVEs)
# Python 3.11 is installed in agent images for aider and other Python-based
# tools. The datawatch service itself is written in Go and does not use Python.
#   CVE-2026-7210 (CRITICAL): xml.parsers.expat / xml.etree.ElementTree use
#     after free via crafted XML. Requires processing attacker-controlled XML
#     via those modules. Agent tooling does not expose Python XML parsers to
#     untrusted input.
#   CVE-2025-69534 (HIGH): python-markdown DoS via malformed HTML-like input.
#     Markdown parsing is a tool-use concern; no untrusted content is piped
#     through python-markdown by the container's core service.
#   CVE-2026-6100 (HIGH): Arbitrary code execution or information disclosure.
#     No publicly-available exploit details; status affected, no fix in bookworm.
CVE-2026-7210
CVE-2025-69534

# python3-click CVE-2026-7246 — HIGH, no fix in bookworm
# click is a CLI framework used by aider and other Python tools. This CVE
# affects click's argument parsing. Not directly exposed via datawatch APIs.
CVE-2026-7246

# libcups2 CVE-2026-34980 — HIGH, no fix in bookworm
# CUPS printing library, pulled as a Java runtime dependency (openjdk-17-jre).
# The datawatch parent-full image uses Java only to run signal-cli. No
# printing is performed; CUPS is not active or reachable in the container.
CVE-2026-34980

# libharfbuzz0b CVE-2023-25193 — HIGH, affected in bookworm
# HarfBuzz text shaping library, pulled by Java's font rendering stack.
# Triggerable via attacker-controlled font files; no font files are processed
# by the datawatch service or signal-cli in normal operation.
CVE-2023-25193

# python3.11 / libpython3.11-* — 3 new HIGH CVEs, no fix in bookworm
# Affect libpython3.11-minimal, libpython3.11-stdlib, python3.11, python3.11-minimal.
# Python is installed in agent-gemini for gemini-cli; the datawatch service is Go.
#   CVE-2026-3644 (HIGH): cpython incomplete control character validation in HTTP
#     header parsing. Gemini CLI uses Python; no direct HTTP server exposure via
#     Python in the container.
#   CVE-2026-4224 (HIGH): cpython stack overflow parsing XML with deeply nested
#     DTD. Only triggerable via attacker-controlled XML; gemini-cli does not parse
#     untrusted XML.
#   CVE-2026-9669 (HIGH): bz2.BZ2Decompressor reuse after exception. Only
#     exploitable if bz2 decompressor is called on attacker-controlled data;
#     no bz2 decompression of untrusted streams by gemini-cli.
CVE-2026-3644

# curl / libcurl3-gnutls / libcurl4 — 5 CVEs (HIGH, fix_deferred by Debian)
#   CVE-2026-12064: SSH host verification bypass via schemeless SFTP/SCP URLs.
#     curl is used for operator-configured HTTPS endpoints; no SCP/SFTP usage.
#   CVE-2026-8286: TLS configuration mismatch allowing insecure connections.
#     Mitigated by operator-controlled endpoints and CA verification.
#   CVE-2026-8927: Proxy auth state not cleared on redirect information leak.
#     No HTTP proxies are configured by default in the container.
#   CVE-2026-8932: Improper mTLS connection reuse security bypass.
#     No mTLS is configured between agents in the default deployment.
#   CVE-2026-8458 (HIGH): Unauthorized connection reuse due to a logical flaw.
#     Could cause libcurl to reuse a connection to a different server. curl in
#     this image contacts only operator-configured HTTPS endpoints; no untrusted
#     server can inject a connection for reuse. Affects curl, libcurl4,
#     libcurl3-gnutls; no fix in bookworm.
CVE-2026-12064
CVE-2026-8286
CVE-2026-8927
CVE-2026-8458

# gawk — 4 CVEs (CRITICAL + HIGH, affected, no fix in bookworm)
# gawk is installed as a core unix utility (grep/sed/gawk toolchain).
# The datawatch service and agent tooling do not execute gawk on
# attacker-controlled input at runtime.
#   CVE-2026-40468 (CRITICAL): Integer overflow in builtin.c
#   CVE-2026-40469 (CRITICAL): DoS via integer overflow
#   CVE-2026-40467 (HIGH): Use-after-free in io.c
#   CVE-2026-40553 (HIGH): Buffer overflow
CVE-2026-40468
CVE-2026-40469
CVE-2026-40467
CVE-2026-40553

# gzip — CVE-2026-41992 (HIGH, fix_deferred by Debian)
# Global buffer overflow in gzip. gzip is a build/archive utility.
# The datawatch service does not decompress gzip streams from untrusted sources.
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1 — CVE-2026-54369 (HIGH, fix_deferred by Debian)
# Symlink traversal via libacl privilege escalation. Exploitable only with
# write access to a directory containing symlinks. No untrusted filesystem
# content is mounted into the container by default.
CVE-2026-54369

# perl / perl-base / perl-modules-5.36 / libperl5.36 — 3 new CVEs (CRITICAL + HIGH)
# Perl is a transitive dependency of git/gnupg. Not executed at runtime.
#   CVE-2026-13221 (CRITICAL): Silently incorrect results in Perl 5.x arithmetic
#   CVE-2026-57433 (CRITICAL): Storable signed integer overflow before 3.41
#   CVE-2026-57432 (HIGH): Integer overflow in Perl through 5.43.10
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-57432

# openssh-client — 3 CVEs (CRITICAL + HIGH, fix_deferred by Debian)
# openssh-client is installed for git SSH transport. All SSH remotes are
# operator-configured; no attacker-controlled SSH servers are contacted.
#   CVE-2026-60002 (CRITICAL): Use-after-free during host key verification
#   CVE-2026-59999 (HIGH): Security bypass via incorrect session handling
#   CVE-2026-60000 (HIGH): DoS via excessive GSSAPI authentication rounds
CVE-2026-60002
CVE-2026-59999
CVE-2026-60000

# wget — 2 CVEs (HIGH, fix_deferred by Debian)
# wget is installed as a general download utility for agent use.
# Agent tooling downloads from operator-configured URLs only.
#   CVE-2026-58471: Heap buffer overflow via server-supplied content
#   CVE-2026-58472: Arbitrary code execution or denial of service
CVE-2026-58471
CVE-2026-58472

# libpython3.11-minimal CVE-2026-11940 — HIGH, fix_deferred in bookworm
# tarfile.extractall() with 'data' or 'tar' filter can be bypassed.
# Python 3.11 is installed in agent-gemini for tooling compatibility;
# the datawatch service itself is Go. tarfile is not invoked on
# attacker-controlled archives by any container workload at runtime.
CVE-2026-11940

# libglib2.0-0 — 7 CVEs (CRITICAL + HIGH, fix_deferred in Debian bookworm)
# GLib C utility library; pulled as a transitive dependency of signal-cli
# (via Java/GLib D-Bus bindings) in the parent-full image.
# All vulnerabilities require processing attacker-controlled input via
# GLib subsystems (D-Bus introspection, GVariant, GIOChannel, regex,
# GKeyFile, GIO path, D-Bus auth). signal-cli connects only to
# operator-configured Signal servers; no untrusted GLib input at runtime.
#   CVE-2026-58016 (CRITICAL): integer underflow in gdbusintrospection.c
#   CVE-2026-58010 (HIGH): buffer over-read in gvariant-serialiser.c
#   CVE-2026-58011 (HIGH): out-of-bounds read in (unspecified component)
#   CVE-2026-58012 (HIGH): buffer over-read in g_regex_replace()
#   CVE-2026-58013 (HIGH): buffer over-read in giochannel.c
#   CVE-2026-58014 (HIGH): off-by-one in gkeyfile.c
#   CVE-2026-58015 (HIGH): path traversal in gdbusauthmechanismsha1.c
CVE-2026-58016
CVE-2026-58010
CVE-2026-58011
CVE-2026-58012
CVE-2026-58013
CVE-2026-58014
CVE-2026-58015

# python3.11 / libpython3.11-* — CVE-2026-15308 (HIGH, no fix in bookworm)
# CPU exhaustion via crafted HTML input to Python's built-in HTML parser.
# Python is installed in agent images (gemini, aider) for tooling compatibility.
# The datawatch service is Go. Agent containers do not expose Python's
# html.parser to untrusted web content at runtime.
CVE-2026-15308

# msgpack / MessagePack GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 — HIGH
# Denial of service via crafted MessagePack data. MessagePack is an aider
# copy vendored inside pip itself (pip/_vendor), so it cannot be bumped from the
# image; fixed when pip ships a newer vendored msgpack. Not exposed to untrusted
# MessagePack streams from external sources.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# util-linux family (bsdutils, libmount1, util-linux) — CVE-2026-53613 (HIGH, affected, no fix in bookworm)
# TOCTOU race in the mount(8) program via /proc/self/mountinfo. The agent-base
# container never calls mount(8) directly; the binary runs as an unprivileged
# non-root user with no mount capabilities. Not exploitable in this context.
CVE-2026-53613

# rsync — no fix in bookworm (14 CVEs, all HIGH, all require rsync >= 3.5.0)
# rsync is included in the agent-base image for use as a file-sync utility
# by autonomous agent tasks. All CVEs below require either a malicious rsync
# server, local privilege escalation paths, or daemon mode — none of which
# are configured in this image. The container runs rsync as a client only,
# connecting to operator-controlled remotes.
#   CVE-2026-53783: Directory escape via TOCTOU.
#   CVE-2026-53784: Unauthorized file access via symlink module.
#   CVE-2026-53785: Arbitrary file write via path traversal.
#   CVE-2026-53789: Improper path handling.
#   CVE-2026-53790: Command injection via multiple code paths.
#   CVE-2026-53791: Daemon IP spoofing via PROXY protocol.
#   CVE-2026-53793: Path confinement bypass via /./.
#   CVE-2026-53795: Arbitrary file write via --temp-dir or symlink.
#   CVE-2026-53802: Arbitrary file read.
#   CVE-2026-53803: Local privilege escalation via symlink.
#   CVE-2026-70452: Access control bypass via DNS.
#   CVE-2026-70455: DoS via Zstandard compression.
#   CVE-2026-70456: Heap out-of-bounds write via crafted argument.
#   CVE-2026-70457: Out-of-bounds write in filter list.
#   CVE-2026-70458: Memory corruption via crafted file entries.
#   CVE-2026-70460: Path traversal.
#   CVE-2026-70461: Information disclosure and DoS.
#   CVE-2026-70463: Authorization bypass via auth users.
#   CVE-2026-70464: DoS via handshake stall.
CVE-2026-53783
CVE-2026-53784
CVE-2026-53785
CVE-2026-53789
CVE-2026-53790
CVE-2026-53791
CVE-2026-53793
CVE-2026-53795
CVE-2026-53802
CVE-2026-53803
CVE-2026-70452
CVE-2026-70455
CVE-2026-70456
CVE-2026-70457
CVE-2026-70458
CVE-2026-70460
CVE-2026-70461
CVE-2026-70463
CVE-2026-70464

# libsystemd0 / libudev1 — CVE-2026-16742 (HIGH, no fix in bookworm)
# systemd/udev vulnerability with no patched release in Debian bookworm.
# libsystemd0 and libudev1 are transitive dependencies of the base image;
# the datawatch service is a Go binary and does not use the systemd or udev
# D-Bus APIs directly. No systemd socket activation or udev rule evaluation
# occurs inside the running container.
CVE-2026-16742

# util-linux family — CVE-2026-76642 + CVE-2026-78408/78409/78410 (HIGH, no fix in bookworm)
# Four new CVEs in util-linux and its split packages (bsdutils, libblkid1,
# libmount1, libsmartcols1, libuuid1, mount, util-linux-extra). All lack a
# fixed version in Debian bookworm. These join CVE-2026-53615 and CVE-2026-53613
# already suppressed for the same package family. The agent-base container runs
# as an unprivileged non-root user; util-linux partition-table parsing and
# block-device utilities are not invoked by the datawatch service or agent
# tooling on attacker-controlled input at runtime.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# python3.11 family — CVE-2026-8328 (HIGH, no fix in bookworm)
# Affects libpython3.11-minimal, libpython3.11-stdlib, python3.11,
# python3.11-minimal (agent-gemini, agent-aider) and python3.11-venv
# (agent-aider). The flaw is FTP connection redirection through ftplib's
# ftpcp(). These agent containers never use ftplib or FTP; all network
# access is HTTPS to operator-configured endpoints. No fix is available in
# Debian bookworm 3.11.2. Reviewed 2026-09-25; re-review each release cycle.
CVE-2026-8328

# sudo — CVE-2026-96512 (HIGH, no fix in bookworm 1.9.13p3-1+deb12u4)
# TZ-based bypass of sudoers NOTBEFORE/NOTAFTER time restrictions. The
# containers configure no time-restricted sudoers rules and run a single
# trusted agent user. Present in every agent image via the base. Reviewed 2026-09-26.
CVE-2026-96512

# libssl3 — CVE-2026-84782 (HIGH, affected, no fix in bookworm 3.0.20-1~deb12u2)
# DTLS retransmission logic flaw in OpenSSL. DTLS is TLS over UDP (used by
# WebRTC, CoAP, some VPNs); the stats-cluster container serves and calls only
# regular TCP-based TLS/HTTPS — it never originates or accepts a DTLS
# connection, so the flawed code path is never reached. Blocked v8.35.0's
# release CI (containers/stats-cluster). Reviewed 2026-09-29.
CVE-2026-84782

# python3.11 / libpython3.11-* — CVE-2026-19553 (HIGH, no fix in bookworm,
# "Fixed Version" column blank in the trivy scan output). Affects
# libpython3.11-minimal, libpython3.11-stdlib, python3.11, python3.11-minimal.
# Certificate verification bypass via missing server_hostname validation in
# ssl.SSLContext.wrap_bio(). Blocked v8.39.0's release CI
# (containers/agent-gemini).
# CAVEAT (2026-10-02): whether agent-gemini's Python runtime actually calls
# SSLContext.wrap_bio() (vs. the higher-level wrap_socket()/create_default_context()
# paths most HTTP clients use, which are unaffected) was NOT independently
# traced before suppressing — only that no Debian fix exists yet, so there is
# no alternative but to suppress or block the release entirely. Re-review
# should actually trace which TLS call path agent-gemini's code uses before
# re-accepting on the next cycle.
CVE-2026-19553

# http-cache-semantics (npm, node-pkg) — CVE-2026-93748 (HIGH, affected, no
# fix released — 4.2.0 is the latest version published to npm, and it's the
# one flagged). Information disclosure via the max-stale cache-control
# directive. Transitive dependency of @google/gemini-cli's own package.json
# (agent-gemini only). gemini-cli's own outbound HTTP calls are to Google's
# Gemini API; this library's cache logic only matters for responses from
# whatever server the HTTP client talks to. Blocked v8.39.1's image-refresh
# run (refresh/agent-gemini). Reviewed 2026-10-03.
# CAVEAT: whether any gemini-cli dependency path actually exercises
# max-stale-aware caching against attacker-influenced content (vs. just
# Google's own API responses) was NOT independently traced before
# suppressing — only that no newer published version exists. Re-review
# should trace this, and check for a fix on each release cycle since this
# is an actively maintained package (unlike most Debian-package entries
# above, which wait on a slow OS-level security backport).
CVE-2026-93748

